<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- msvc-pin.props: THE ONE COMPILER. Written 2026-11-21 by Melanikus (Frost) for the AvP port, Bishop for the owner after alpha.3 ("FIXING, NOT PATCHING").

     WHY: alpha.3's libsmackerenc.dll and mp4-to-smk.exe were each flagged by one antivirus engine; the same code built here scanned 0 of 71. The one
     difference was the compiler: GitHub's runner image (windows-2025-vs2026 20261116.315) had moved to MSVC 14.52.37025 under us, and this project
     builds with 14.51.36231. The same source gave other machine code (the Rich header, the linker version, .text's size), so what shipped was never
     what had been scanned. Pinning one exact compiler, on every machine, makes a build here and a build on CI the same bytes (with the deterministic
     flags each project sets), so the files scanned clean are the files that ship.

     WHAT: every project that ships imports this file after Microsoft.Cpp.Default.props and before Microsoft.Cpp.props. VCToolsVersion chooses the
     MSVC folder (VC\Tools\MSVC\<version>) the whole build uses: compiler, linker and libraries. Microsoft.Cpp.props fills it in with the newest
     installed one only when it is empty (Microsoft.Cpp.VCTools.props); set before Microsoft.Cpp.Default.props, a developer prompt would clear it
     (ClearDevCommandPromptEnvVars). The build FAILS, saying why, if the version is anything else (a /p:VCToolsVersion on the command line included)
     or that MSVC is not installed: it is never quietly built with another.

     TO MOVE IT: change AvpxMsvcVersion here, install that MSVC on every machine that builds (Visual Studio Installer, the "MSVC v145 build tools" of
     that version), build, and have the result scanned before anything ships. CI installs the same version from Microsoft's own installer. -->
<Project xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/developer/msbuild/2003">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <AvpxMsvcVersion>14.51.36231</AvpxMsvcVersion>
    <VCToolsVersion>$(AvpxMsvcVersion)</VCToolsVersion>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <Target Name="AvpxMsvcPinCheck" BeforeTargets="PrepareForBuild">
    <Error Condition="'$(VCToolsVersion)' != '$(AvpxMsvcVersion)'" Text="This build must use MSVC $(AvpxMsvcVersion) (msvc-pin.props), and it was asked for $(VCToolsVersion)." />
    <Error Condition="!Exists('$(VCToolsInstallDir)bin\Hostx64\x86\cl.exe') and !Exists('$(VCToolsInstallDir)bin\Hostx86\x86\cl.exe')" Text="MSVC $(AvpxMsvcVersion) is not installed here (no compiler in $(VCToolsInstallDir)): install it with the Visual Studio Installer, as msvc-pin.props says." />
  </Target>
</Project>
